course: dictionary
lesson: 5430
title: Laid: the past of lay
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Laid is the past of the verb lay. To lay something means to put it down carefully, often flat. «She laid the baby in the cot.» This happened in the past, so we write laid.
explain: Laid can mean more than one thing. «The hen laid an egg.» Here a bird made an egg. «Laid the table» means put the plates and cutlery on it, ready for a meal.
explain: In an informal phrase, «laid back» means calm and relaxed. Context tells you which meaning is right: is someone putting something down, making an egg, or just feeling calm?
fact: Laid is the past of lay: lay, laid, laying.
fact: «Laid» means put down carefully, often flat.
fact: Birds, reptiles, fish and insects lay eggs, so «laid» can mean an egg was made.
fact: «Rock layers are laid one on top of another, so lower layers are usually older.»
fact: «Laid back» is an informal phrase meaning calm and relaxed.
exercise: «The roots of one rye plant, laid end to end, were measured at over 600 kilometres.» What does laid mean here? | *Placed in a line, one end to the next | Put on a plate for dinner | Calm and relaxed | Hatched from an egg
exercise: Which sentence uses laid to mean that a bird made an egg? | He is laid back at the weekend | The baby was laid to sleep | She laid the book on the desk | *The hen laid an egg
exercise: Fill the gap: Dad ___ the plates on the table. | lie | lay | *laid | laying
test: What is the past of lay? | lie | lays | laying | *laid
test: What does «laid back» mean? | Made of eggs | Laid out for a meal | *Calm and relaxed | Put down flat
exam: «Rock layers are laid one on top of another.» In this sentence, laid means | Calm and relaxed | Broken into small pieces | *Put down in order, one on top of another | Hatched from eggs
